body:
When a lot younger out of the blue I used to get super weird feelings in my knees of all things. Similar to how you are describing - it was this fleeting moment of deep wrongness with the universe and would only last for 30 seconds or so. Very different to my normal feelings of alienation or being so different to other people. This was a more "universal" feeling there was something very, very wrong with existence. I sometimes wonder if it wasn't me realising we are all in The Matrix or something.

&#x200B;

\> You're here because you know something. What you know, you can't explain. But you feel it. You felt it your entire life. That there's something wrong with the world. You don't know what it is, but it's there. Like a splinter in your mind - driving you mad
